{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "GEN",
  "chapter": 48,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass after these things, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " told Joseph, Behold, thy father ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sick: and he took with him his two sons, Manasseh and Ephraim.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " told Jacob, and said, Behold, thy son Joseph cometh to thee: and Israel strengthened himself, and sat upon the bed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob said to Joseph, God Almighty appeared to me at Luz, in the land of Canaan, and blessed me,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said to me, Behold I will make thee fruitful, and multiply thee, and I will make of thee a multitude of people; and will give this land to thy seed after thee, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an everlasting possession.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now, thy two sons, Ephraim and Manasseh, who were born to thee in the land of Egypt, before I came to thee into Egypt, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine; as Reuben and Simeon, they shall be mine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thy issue, which thou begettest after them, shall be thine, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall be called after the name of their brethren in their inheritance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as for me, when I came from Padan, Rachel died by me in the land of Canaan, in the way, when yet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " but a little way to come to Ephrath: and I buried her there in the way of Ephrath, the same ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Beth-lehem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Israel beheld Joseph's sons, and said, Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " these?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph said to his father, They ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my sons, whom God hath given me in this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ". And he said, Bring them, I pray thee, to me, and I will bless them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Now the eyes of Israel were dim for age, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he could not see:) And he brought them near to him; and he kissed them, and embraced them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Israel said to Joseph, I had not thought to see thy face: and lo, God hath shown me also thy seed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph brought them out from between his knees, and he bowed himself with his face to the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph took them both, Ephraim in his right hand towards Israel's left hand, and Manasseh in his left hand towards Israel's right hand, and brought ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " near to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Israel stretched out his right hand, and laid ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon Ephraim's head, who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the younger, and his left hand upon Manasseh's head, guiding his hands by design; for Manasseh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the first-born.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he blessed Joseph, and said, God, before whom my fathers Abraham and Isaac did walk, the God who hath fed me all my life long to this day,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The angel who hath redeemed me from all evil, bless the lads; and let my name be named on them, and the name of my fathers Abraham and Isaac: and let them grow into a multitude in the midst of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when Joseph saw that his father laid his right hand upon the head of Ephraim, it displeased him: and he lifted his father's hand, to remove it from Ephraim's head to Manasseh's head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph said to his father, Not so, my father; for this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the first-born; put thy right hand upon his head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And his father refused, and said, I know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", my son, I know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; he also shall become a people, and he also shall be great; but truly his younger brother shall be greater than he, and his seed shall become a multitude of nations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he blessed them that day, saying, In thee shall Israel bless, saying, God make thee as Ephraim and as Manasseh: and he set Ephraim before Manasseh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Israel said to Joseph, Behold, I die; but God shall be with you, and bring you again to the land of your fathers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.48.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.48.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover I have given to thee one portion above thy brethren, which I took out of the hand of the Amorite with my sword and with my bow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
